        "Name": "Immersive virtual prism adaptation reshapes visual field representations in the inferior parietal lobule",
        "ReferencesAndLinks": [
          "Link to be added after publication"
        ]
      },
      "readme": "# Immersive virtual prism adaptation reshapes visual field\n# representations in the inferior parietal lobule\n\nFarron N, Wilf M, Perez-Marcos D, Perrin H, Serino A,\nClarke S, Crottaz-Herbette S (2026)\n\n## Study description\nRaw fMRI data from 56 healthy participants who underwent\nvisuomotor adaptation to a rightward visual shift implemented\neither in immersive virtual reality (iVR) or using optical\nprism deviation (OD), with corresponding control conditions.\n\n## Participants\n  sub-01 to sub-16: iVR-shift (n=16)\n  sub-17 to sub-30: iVR-ctrl  (n=14)\n  sub-31 to sub-44: OD-shift  (n=14)\n  sub-45 to sub-58: OD-ctrl   (n=14)\n\n## Sessions\n  ses-01: Pre-adaptation fMRI + structural T1w\n  ses-02: Post-adaptation fMRI\n\n## Task\nVisual detection of targets in left, central or right\nvisual field (task-detection).\n\n## MRI acquisition\niVR groups: TR=2s, TE=30ms, flip=80deg, 64 slices, 2x2x2mm\nOD groups:  TR=2s, TE=30ms, flip=90deg, 32 slices, 3x3x3mm\nT1w: 3D gradient echo, 160 slices, 1x1x1mm\n\n## Contact\nnicolas.farron@chuv.ch\nLausanne University Hospital (CHUV), Switzerland\n",
